<title>CHILE: Mantos Blancos reports higher Q1 net.</title>
<headline>Mantos Blancos reports higher Q1 net.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper mine Mantos Blancos SA reported the following results in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>			    Q1 1997		  Q1 1996</p>
<p> Net profit		   18.1	    profit  7.6</p>
<p> Operating profit	   27.6	    profit 10.6</p>
<p> Non-operating loss	 5.3		 loss  1.3</p>
<p> Total revenues	     78.5		     60.5</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>Mantos Blancos, the only large copper mine traded on Santiago Stock Exchange, reported the results to the Stocks and Securities Superintendent. It is owned 75 percent by Luxembourg-based Minorco SA.</p>
<p>((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-6995595 x211))</p>
